  <prompt>Author a nightly ArchTest that reads the 14-role Infrastructure/Auth/GraphAppRoles.cs constant and queries the UAMI service principal's appRoleAssignments via Graph SDK, failing on mismatch (either missing or extra roles). Sequence into r3 forcing-functions via a coordinated PR with `ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1` per r3 task-042-063-ci-gate-wiring-deferral.md — do NOT edit .github/workflows/** in isolation; author the coord-PR spec at projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/graph-app-role-parity-coord-pr.md.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform test engineer. Expert in Microsoft.Graph SDK v6, appRoleAssignments query patterns, GraphAppRoles.cs constant shape (r3 task 062), and coord-PR authoring for cross-worktree CI wiring. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>File tests/integration/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.NightlyTests/GraphAppRoleParityTest.cs exists as an integration test (nightly cadence, not per-PR) that: (a) reads GraphAppRoles.cs constant reflectively; (b) queries UAMI SP appRoleAssignments via Graph SDK v6 with explicit tenantId; (c) compares the two sets; (d) fails with a diff-formatted message if missing or extra. Coord-PR spec at notes/graph-app-role-parity-coord-pr.md describes the .github/workflows/** wiring diff for the ci-cd-r1 worktree to apply.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Per spec.md FR-13 + T3 + r3 task 062: GraphAppRoles.cs is a compile-time constant of 14 role IDs the UAMI SP MUST have appRoleAssignments for. Drift (someone revokes a role in Azure Portal, or GraphAppRoles.cs adds a role and H10 hasn't run) is a T3 silent-fail — Graph 403s at runtime. Nightly parity check catches drift within 24h. Per r3 task-042-063-ci-gate-wiring-deferral.md, .github/workflows/** wiring is coordinated with the ci-cd-r1 worktree, not edited in isolation.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.NightlyTests/GraphAppRoleParityTest.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.NightlyTests/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.NightlyTests.csproj</file>
      <file role="new">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/graph-app-role-parity-coord-pr.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Auth/GraphAppRoles.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="005" status="pending">GraphAppRoles.cs 14 GUIDs completed via `az` enumeration (Phase A)</dependency>
      <dependency task="053" status="pending">H10 handler grants roles onto UAMI SP</dependency>
      <dependency task="064" status="pending">ArchTest suite baseline exists (I1-I5)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-13">SCOPE: Test verifies UAMI SP appRoleAssignments equals the GraphAppRoles.cs 14-role set exactly (no missing, no extra).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md T3">SCOPE: This is a silent-fail-trap safety net — T3 (UAMI SP role parity) is normally verified by H10 handler post-condition per FR-13; the nightly test catches drift AFTER provisioning.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md §4D I5">SCOPE: Graph SDK query MUST pass explicit tenantId — no `.default`-only scope; enforces I5.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">SCOPE: Integration test (nightly cadence, NOT per-PR — Graph API latency + rate limits make per-PR untenable); sequenced into r3 KEEP paths per ADR-038 §7.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: Coord-PR spec at notes/graph-app-role-parity-coord-pr.md describes the .github/workflows/** wiring diff for ci-cd-r1 to apply; do NOT edit .github/workflows/** in this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: Test failure message MUST be a diff (missing roles + extra roles listed by displayName + GUID) so the operator can act without reading a debugger.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§6.5">SCOPE: Coordinated PR with ci-cd-r1 is Path C compliance (ci-workflows=Y per hot-path declaration); do NOT unilaterally merge to .github/workflows/**.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: NFR-09 — Graph SDK v6 / Kiota 2.0 error type; catch ODataError (not ServiceException); ResponseStatusCode is int; ResponseHeaders is dict.</constraint>
  </constraints>

