  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Load spec.md FR-13 + T3 + NFR-09 + r3 task-042-063-ci-gate-wiring-deferral.md.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Read constant">Read GraphAppRoles.cs — enumerate the (Resource, AppRoleId, DisplayName) tuples.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Scaffold project">Create tests/integration/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.NightlyTests/ .csproj referencing BFF project (for GraphAppRoles.cs constant) + Microsoft.Graph v6 + xUnit.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Test">Author GraphAppRoleParityTest.cs — reflectively read GraphAppRoles.cs; construct Graph client with explicit tenantId (I5); query GET /servicePrincipals/{uami-sp-id}/appRoleAssignments; compare sets; assert equality; on failure, emit diff.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Error handling">Wrap Graph calls in try/catch ODataError (Graph v6 / Kiota 2.0 error type per NFR-09) — surface ResponseStatusCode + first-line message.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Coord-PR spec">Write notes/graph-app-role-parity-coord-pr.md describing the .github/workflows/** wiring: a nightly-scheduled workflow that runs `dotnet test tests/integration/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.NightlyTests/` with auth secrets from GH Actions secrets; env-vars UAMI_SP_OBJECT_ID + AZURE_TENANT_ID.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Verify local">dotnet build + dotnet test the nightly project against dev tenant/UAMI — verify parity check works.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Deviations">Document any deviation in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Index update">Update TASK-INDEX.md: task 067 → ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the Graph SDK v6 / Kiota 2.0 query for appRoleAssignments returns an unexpected shape, OR if the ci-cd-r1 worktree responds to the coord-PR with a scope conflict that would delay wiring beyond Phase F acceptance, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6. Do NOT unilaterally edit .github/workflows/** to bypass coord (that would violate the r3 handoff constraint).</trigger>
