  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">GraphAppRoleParityTest reads all 14 (Resource, AppRoleId, DisplayName) tuples from GraphAppRoles.cs reflectively.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the UAMI SP has exactly the 14 role IDs in GraphAppRoles.cs, when the test runs, then it PASSES.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the UAMI SP is missing 1+ role IDs, when the test runs, then it FAILS with a diff message listing the missing roles by displayName + GUID.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the UAMI SP has 1+ extra role IDs beyond GraphAppRoles.cs, when the test runs, then it FAILS with a diff message listing the extra roles.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Graph SDK query passes an explicit tenantId parameter (I5 compliance); ArchTest I5 in task 064 does NOT flag this test as a violation.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Graph exceptions are caught as ODataError (Graph v6 / Kiota 2.0 per NFR-09), not ServiceException.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Coord-PR spec at notes/graph-app-role-parity-coord-pr.md describes the .github/workflows/** wiring (nightly cron schedule + auth env-vars); does NOT edit workflow files directly.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0 (against dev tenant); zero analyzer warnings.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

